    {
      "id": "public-home-context",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Repo Context",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 980,
        "y": 760
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 380,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Publish only what is ready to be read\n\nThis repository should hold work that can stand in daylight: clear documents, reliable examples, reusable node classes, and artifacts that represent the taste of the system well. Public does not mean exhaustive. It means chosen.\n\n## Signal taste through structure\n\nTreat the public repo as a front door. It should communicate discipline through naming, hierarchy, visual polish, and explanatory strength. Let the public surface tell people what Twilite values before they read a line of implementation detail.\n\n## Use public to invite, not to dump\n\nPublish patterns, examples, notes, and interfaces that invite collaborators into the world. The public layer should be hospitable and persuasive. It should never feel like a storage bucket for everything that happened to compile.\n\n## Summary\n\nPublic is the front porch: deliberate, readable, and hospitable. Put the work here when it is ready to represent the architect in full view.",
        "definitionKey": "markdown",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "markdown",
          "sourceRef": "/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node",
          "ref": "/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        },
        "_bridge": {
          "classKey": "markdown",
          "classRef": "/library/classes/nodes/markdown.node-class.node"
        }
      }
    },
